  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to creation of decent and productive jobs for improved livelihoods</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Government of Malawi, in consultation with social partners, is mainstreaming decent employment outcomes into national development processes and plans through the revision and formulation of a comprehensive national job creation strategy. The National Job Creation strategy is addressing the following issues: improving access to affordable capital, promoting trade and exports, improving infrastructure and energy services, improving skills development especially for youth, improving legal and policy environment, promoting industrial production, accelerating transformation of the agricultural sector, strengthening institutional capacity for managing labour and sustaining job creation, minimising negative impacts of post COVID-19 on industry&#x2019;s productivity and job creation. The expected outcomes include a pro-employment economic development agenda requires that job creation should be mainstreamed across all sectors of the economy. 
In addition to the foregoing, the Strategy is contributing towards achieving the following outcomes: Improved access to finance; Improved access to business equipment; Reduced cost of finance; Domestic trade promoted; Exports promoted; Improved ICT services; Improved transport infrastructure; Improved energy supply; Improved skills development; Increased access to labour market information; Increased industrial production; Increased tourism; Sustainable and productive indigenous MSMEs and large enterprises; Enhanced sound macroeconomic and public finance management; A regulated and enabling business environment and accelerated agriculture. 
The intervention is being implemented in partnership with Government line Ministries, United Nations, Private sector, communities and other cooperating partners. 
Beneficiaries of the intervention include the people of Malawi especially youth and women.</narrative>
  </description>
